# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DUBAI XTRA - .gitignore
#
# Repo root = WordPress install root.
# When Cloudways pulls this repo into public_html/, the theme files
# land at public_html/wp-content/themes/dubai-xtra-child/ automatically
# with no deploy script. WordPress core, third-party plugins, the
# parent theme, uploads, caches, and logs are all server-managed and
# never enter the repo.
#
# Strategy: deny everything by default, then explicitly un-ignore the
# bits we own (custom theme + project docs + future custom plugins).
#
# Audit performed against the actual project tree on 2026-05-01.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Default: ignore everything ─────────────────────────────────────
/*
/.*

# ─── Re-include root project files ──────────────────────────────────
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.editorconfig
!.github/
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!LICENSE
!composer.json
!composer.lock
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# ─── Walk into wp-content -> themes -> our theme ────────────────────
# Each level is un-ignored explicitly so git recurses into it. Inside
# each level we re-deny everything else so siblings (default themes,
# third-party plugins, uploads, etc.) stay out.
!/wp-content/
/wp-content/*
!/wp-content/themes/
/wp-content/themes/*
!/wp-content/themes/dubai-xtra-child/

# Once we're inside our theme, everything is tracked by default.
# Defensive excludes for build tooling / editor junk / logs are below.

# ─── Custom mu-plugins (allow if/when we add any) ───────────────────
!/wp-content/mu-plugins/

# ─── Custom plugins (uncomment + add path when we build one) ────────
# !/wp-content/plugins/dubai-xtra-core/

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEFENSIVE EXCLUDES
# Things we never want committed even when they appear inside an
# otherwise-allowed path (e.g. node_modules inside the theme).
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Editor + OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.vs/
**/*.code-workspace
**/*.sublime-project
**/*.sublime-workspace
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# ─── Build artifacts / dependency dirs ──────────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
**/vendor/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.cache/
**/.parcel-cache/
**/.next/
**/.nuxt/

# ─── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
**/debug.log
**/error_log
**/error.log

# ─── Env + secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# ─── Test snapshots / coverage ──────────────────────────────────────
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
**/__snapshots__/

# ─── ACF local JSON sync ────────────────────────────────────────────
# No acf-json/ folder exists in the theme today (we register fields
# programmatically via inc/acf-fields.php). If you later enable ACF's
# local JSON sync, the acf-json/ folder under the theme is ALREADY
# allowed by the theme un-ignore above. Field group definitions belong
# in version control.
